# repo-standard machinery must stay LF on every platform — a CRLF checkout puts \r on
# the shebang line and every hook dies with exit 127. These lines pin only the
# standard's scripts; set your own policy for the rest of the repo as you see fit.
.claude/hooks/* text eol=lf
.githooks/* text eol=lf
bin/track text eol=lf
bin/register text eol=lf
# The tracker-hwm sidecar is data, not a script, but a CRLF checkout used to zero its
# recorded high-water marks and re-mint deleted IDs (B47). Unpathed on purpose: the
# sidecar lives next to whatever TRACKER_FILE points at, so the pin must match at any depth.
tracker-hwm text eol=lf
